  "slug": "memories-networks-realistic-48a0",
  "summary": "Six November 2026 preprints apply thermodynamic, non-Hermitian and control-theoretic tools to steady states, thermometry, heat engines and driven phonon dynamics.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is the use of thermodynamic and dynamical-systems concepts to characterize or steer many-body quantum systems. Phonon hydrodynamics is cast as a non-Hermitian symmetry-breaking transition, with exceptional points bounding the hydrodynamic window. Information thermodynamics links extractable work to quantum properties of closed systems in microscopic thermal equilibrium. Fock-space current engineering stabilizes selectable bosonic Fock states via a stationary current-balance law. k-local Hamiltonians improve equilibrium thermometry over 2-local models, approaching the heat-capacity optimum as locality grows. A Bose-Hubbard Otto-cycle machine uses interaction changes to enhance heat performance. Differentiable optimization and recurrent networks predict and control light-driven electron-phonon dynamics in a two-site model. The items are heterogeneous in platform, but converge on engineered control and thermodynamic resource accounting.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
}
